SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The mmeemmffdd__ccrreeaattee() function is expected to be compatible with the Linux
     system call of the same name.

     The sshhmm__ooppeenn() and sshhmm__uunnlliinnkk() functions are believed to conform to IEEE
     Std 1003.1b-1993 (“POSIX.1”).

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The mmeemmffdd__ccrreeaattee() function appeared in FreeBSD 13.0.

     The sshhmm__ooppeenn() and sshhmm__uunnlliinnkk() functions first appeared in FreeBSD 4.3.
     The functions were reimplemented as system calls using shared memory ob‐
     jects directly rather than files in FreeBSD 8.0.

     sshhmm__rreennaammee() first appeared in FreeBSD 13.0 as a FreeBSD extension.

